        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T17:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are `java_import` modules allowed to specify the install path? I can\u0027t seem to find any applicable property from go/Android.bp, but please let me know if you are aware of a way to do so.\n\nPersonally I\u0027d prefer introducing this module type, as utilizing `java_import` would require maintaining an additional property struct type and introducing a new dimension (file extension) in determining the module type to generate, making the logic more complex in aosp/3317057.",
      "parentUuid": "f1d580d4_e3061d82",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 874,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "ecd141a7b84b88675f0a6bd2c6c1517dd714ba23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ae444e0_df788f5e",
        "filename": "etc/prebuilt_etc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 874,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T17:16:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Are java_import modules allowed to specify the install path? \n\nI think installation path should not be necessary. All java_imports are installed in [/$partition/framework](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/java.go;l\u003d1031?q\u003dframework%5C%22%20f:build%2Fsoong%20case:yes%20-f:test\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main). Are you noticing cases where they are installed in a different subdirectory?\n\nI think if we were to introduce this module type, we should have a neverallow rule and restrict this to autogenerated modules. \n\nMy worry with introducing these module types is that java_import/android_app_import do some additional checks ([e.g.](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/app_import.go;l\u003d394-444;drc\u003dea147927ac3a674ea61c1b05698a0d7131052d0b?q\u003dandroid_app_import\u0026ct\u003dos\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main) ). Such checks would not run on apps/jars installed using these new module types",
      "parentUuid": "d5ac555c_dfed8076",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 874,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "ecd141a7b84b88675f0a6bd2c6c1517dd714ba23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c093bb64_fa93105b",
        "filename": "etc/prebuilt_etc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 874,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T06:07:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Are you noticing cases where they are installed in a different subdirectory?\n\nMy specific worry is regarding [these](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:vendor/panasonic/hawk/hawk-proprietary.mk;l\u003d205?q\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main%20%5C:.*%5C%2Fframework%5C%2F.*%5C%2F.*%5C.vdex%20%22PRODUCT_COPY_FILES%22) entries. Do `java_import` modules generate vdex files, and if so is it possible to install in these matching directories (`system/framework/oat/\u003cproduct\u003e/*.vdex`)?\n\n\u003e Such checks would not run on apps/jars installed using these new module types\n\nBut aren\u0027t they not being checked on file installed via `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES` regardless? Is your proposal that these entries should not exist in `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES` in the first place and installed as `PRODUCT_PACKAGES`?",
      "parentUuid": "2ae444e0_df788f5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 874,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "ecd141a7b84b88675f0a6bd2c6c1517dd714ba23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9abef9af_14160447",
        "filename": "etc/prebuilt_etc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 874,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T16:49:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The entries in the above example seem to be vdex files. Those prebuilts were generated in 2019, and are almost certain to be rejected on device and require dexopt. \n\n\u003e Is your proposal that these entries should not exist in PRODUCT_COPY_FILES in the first place and installed as PRODUCT_PACKAGES?\n\nI wish we do. I do not see why we should not [generate provenance metadata](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/app_import.go;l\u003d433;drc\u003dea147927ac3a674ea61c1b05698a0d7131052d0b?q\u003dandroid_app_import\u0026ct\u003dos\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main) for these apps/jars\n\nIntroducing these module types would introduce new ways to bypass this",
      "parentUuid": "c093bb64_fa93105b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 874,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "ecd141a7b84b88675f0a6bd2c6c1517dd714ba23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27b13ee1_64a99efc",
        "filename": "etc/prebuilt_etc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 874,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-01T21:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this out. IIUC your concern is mainly two points:\n\n1. Installing jar files via PRODUCT_COPY_FILES\n2. Introducing prebuilt_* module types to support 1.\n\nRegarding 1.: I agree with you in that this is problematic. However given that the purpose of this changes stack is converting `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES` and is not about evaluating the validity of the entries in `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES`, I believe that this concern is out of scope of this change. However, I\u0027d be happy to discuss more about how to rectify this in other changes.\n\nRegarding 2.: I have created [this topic](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22auto_generated_neverallow%22) to prevent this module type from being defined in Android.bp files.",
      "parentUuid": "9abef9af_14160447",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 874,
